## Key Takeaways

* Monitoring protects AI performance after release.
* Evaluation and monitoring serve different purposes.
* AI quality can change after deployment.
* Policy and model changes require controlled validation.
* User feedback is an important source of production evidence.
* Not every feedback item is a defect.
* Critical AI and security issues require immediate escalation.
* Continuous improvement should follow a controlled lifecycle.
* Production metrics must have measurable thresholds and owners.
* Business outcomes matter as much as technical performance.
